{
  "title": "Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اﷲ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE \nPeace be on you, O Abu Abdillah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللهِ\nASSALAAMO A’ALAYKA YABNA RASOOLIL LAAHE \nPeace be on you, O son of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَابْنَ اَمِیْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA AMEERIL MOMENEENA \nPeace be on you, O son of the Commander of the Faithful \nوَ ابْنَ سَیِّدِ الْوَصِیِّیْنَ\nWABNA SAYYEDIL WASIYYEENA \nand the son of the chief of the successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَابْنَ فَاطِمَۃَ سَیِّدَۃِ نِسَآءِ الْعَالَمِیْنَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA FAATEMAATA SAYYEDATE NESAAAIL A’ALAMEENA \nPeace be on you, O son of Fatima, the chief of the women of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا خِیَرَۃَ اللهِ وَابْنَ خِیَرَتِهٖ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA KHEYARATAL LAAHE WABNA KHEYARATEHI \nSalutation on you O the good creation of Allah and the son of His best creation!\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا ثَارَ اللهِ وَابْنَ ثاَرِهٖ وَ الْوِتْرَ الْمَوْتُوْرَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA SAARAL LAAHE WABNA SAAREHI WAL WITRAL MAWTOORA \nPeace be on you, O fearless warrior of Allah, the son of His fearless warrior, the one who was alone, and wronged by the murder of relatives. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ وَ عَلَی الْأَرْوَاحِ الَّتِیْ حَلَّتْ بِفِنَآئِكَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA WA A’LAL ARWAAHIL LATEE HALLAT BE FENAA-EKA \nPeace be on you, and on the souls who died with you.\nعَلَیْكُمْ مِنِّی جَمِیْعًا سَلَامُ اللهِ اَبَدًا\nA’LAYKUM MINNEE JAMEE-A’N SALAAMUL LAAHE ABADAM \nI send peace of AIlah on all of you forever, \nمَا بَقِیْتُ وَ بَقِیَ اللَّیْلُ وَ النَّهَارُ\nMAA BAQEETO WA BAQEYAL LAYLO WAN NAHAARO \nso long as I remain alive, and the night and day remains.\nیَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ\nYAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE \nO Abu Abdillah, \nلَقَدْ عَظُمَتِ الرَّزِیَّۃُ وَ جَلَّتْ \nLAQAD A’ZOMATIR RAZIYYATO WA JALLAT \ngreat is the loss, and unbearable \nوَ عَظُمَتِ الْمُصِیْبَۃُ بِكَ عَلَیْنَا\nWA A’ZOMATIL MOSEEBATO BEKA A’LAYNAA \nand great is your tragedy for us,\nوَ عَلی جَمِیْعِ اَهْلِ اْلاِسْلَامِ\nWA A’LAA JAMEE-E’ AHLIL ISLAAME \nand for all the people of Islam,\nوَ جَلَّتْ وَ عَظُمَتْ مُصِیْبَتُكَ فِیْ السَّموَاتِ عَلی جَمِیْعِ اَهْلِ السَّمَاوَاتِ\nWA JALLAT WA A’ZOMAT MOSEEBATOKA FIS SAMAAWAATE A’LAA JAMEE-E’ AHLIS SAMAAWAATE \nand unbearable and great is your tragedy in the heavens, and for all the dwellers of the heavens.\nفَلَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّۃً اَسَّسَتْ اَسَاسَ الظُّلْمِ وَ الْجَوْرِ عَلَیْكُمْ اَهْلَ الْبَیْتِ\nFA-LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN ASSASAT ASAASAZ ZULME WAL JAWRE A’LAYKUM AHLAL BAYTE \nMay Allah curse the people who laid the basis of oppression, and the wrongs done against you, people of the House\nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّۃً دَفَعَتْكُمْ عَنْ مَقَامِكُمْ\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN DAFA-A’TKUM A’N MOQAAMEKUM \nMay Allah curse who tried to obscure and deny your office and status,\nوَ اَزَالَتْكُمْ عَنْ مَرَاتِبِكُمُ الَّتِیْ رَتَّبَكُمُ اللهُ فِیْهَا\nWA AZAALATKUM A’N MARAATEBOKOMUL LATEE RATTABAKOMUL LAAHO FEEHAA \nwillfully neglected your rank and class Allah had made known in clear terms.\nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّۃً قَتَلَتْكُمْ\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN QATALATKUM \nMay Allah curse the people who killed you, \nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ الْمُمَهِّدِیْنَ لَهُمْ\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHUL MOMAH-HEDEENA LAHUM \nand those who made it easy for them, \nبِالتَّمْكِیْنِ مِنْ قِتَالِكُمْ\nBIT-TAMKEENE MIN QETAALEKUM \nby preparing the grounds for your killing.\nبَرِئْتُ اِلَی اللهِ وَ اِلَیْكُمْ مِنْهُمْ\nBAREA-TO ELAL LAAHE WA ELAYKUM MINHUM \nI turn to you and Allah, away from them,\nوَ مِنْ اَشْیَاعِهِمْ وَ اَتْبَاعِهِمْ وَ اَوْلِیَآئِهِمْ\nWA MIN ASHYAA-E’HIM WA ATBAA-E’HIM WA AWLEYAAEHIM \nand their adherents, their followers, and their friends.\nیَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ\nYAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE \nO Abu Abdillah,\nاِنِّیْ سِلْمٌ لِمَنْ سَالَمَكُمْ\nINNEE SILMUN LEMAN SAALAMAKUM \nI am at peace with those who make peace with you,\nوَ حَرْبٌ لِمَنْ حَارَبَكُمْ اِلی یَوْمِ الْقِیَامَۃِ\nWA HARBUN LEMAN HAARABAKUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE \nAnd I am at war with those who make war with you, till the Day of Judgement.\nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ آلَ زِیَادٍ وَ آلَ مَرْوَانَ\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO AALA ZEYAADIN WA AALA MARWAANA \nAnd may Allah cruse the family of Ziyaad and the family of Marwaan; \nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ بَنِیْ اُمَیَّۃَ قَاطِبَۃً\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO BANEE UMAYYATA QAATEBATAN \nAnd may Allah curse the group and the tribe of Umiyyah, one and all, altogether;\nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ ابْنَ مَرْجَانَۃَ\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHUBNA MARJAANATA \nAnd may Allah cruse Ibne Marjanah \nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ عُمَرَبْنَ سَعْدٍ\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO O’MARABNA SAA’DIN \nAnd may Allah curse Umar ibne Sa`ad, \nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ شِمْرًا\nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO SHIMRAN \nand may Allah curse Shimr\nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّۃً اَسْرَجَتْ \nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN ASRAJAT \nAnd may Allah curse the nation that saddled up, \nوَ اَلْجَمَتْ وَ تَنَقَّبَتْ لِقِتَالِكَ\nWA ALJAMAT WA TANAQQABAT LE-QETAALEKA \nreined in, and veiled themselves for the fight against you.\nبِاَبِیْ اَنْتَ وَ اُمِّی لَقَدْ عَظُمَ مُصَابِیْ بِكَ\nBE-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE LAQAD A’ZOMA MOSAABEE BEKA \nMy father and mother be sacrificed for you, great is my sorrow for you.\nفَاَسْئَلُ اللهَ الَّذِیْ اَكْرَمَ مَقَامَكَ\nFA-ASALUL LAAHAL LAZEE AKRAMA MAQAAMAKA \nI pray to Allah who has honoured your status, \nوَ اَكْرَمَنِیْ بِكَ اَنْ یَرْزُقَنِیْ طَلَبَ ثَارِكَ\nWA AKRAMANEE BEKA AYN YARZOQANEE TALABA SAAREKA \nand honoured me through you, to grant me an opportunity\nمَعَ اِمَامٍ مَنْصُوْرٍ مِنْ اَهْلِ بَیْتِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nMA-A’ EMAAMIN MANSOORIN MIN AHLE BAYTE MOHAMMADIN \nto be with a victorious Imam, from the family of Muhammad, \nصَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ آلِهٖ\nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI\nblessings of Allah be on him and his family.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِیْ عِنْدَكَ وَجِیْهًا بِالْحُسَیْنِ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A’LNEE I’NDAKA WAJEEHAN BIL-HUSAYNE \nO Allah, make me worthy of respect with You, through Husayn, \nعَلَیْهِ السَّلَامُ فِیْ الدُّنْیَا وَ اْلآخِرَۃِ\nA’LAYHIS SALAAMO FID-DUNYAA WAL AAAKHERATE \npeace be on him, in this world and the Hereafter.\nیَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ\nYAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE \nO Abu Abdillah, \nاِنِّی اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَی اللهِ\nINNEE ATAQARRABO ELAL LAAHE \nI seek nearness to Allah,\nوَ اِلٰی رَسُوْلِهٖ وَ اِلٰی اَمْیرِ الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ\nWA ELAA RASOOLEHEE WA ELAA AMEERIL MOMENEENA \nand to His Messenger, to the Commander of the Faithful,\nوَ اِلٰی فَاطِمَۃَ وَ اِلَی الْحَسَنِ وَ اِلَیْكَ\nWA ELAA FAATEMATA WA ELAL HASANE WA ELAYKA \nto Fatima, and to Hasan, and to you, \nبِمُوَالَاتِكَ وَ بِالْبَرَآئَۃِ مِمَّنْ قَاتَلَكَ وَ نَصَبَ لَك الْحَرْبَ \nBE-MAWAALAATEKA WA BIL-BARAA-ATE MIMMAN QAATALAKA WA NASABA LAKAL HARBA \nthrough love for you, and disassociating with those who killed you, and prepared to fight you\nوَ بِالْبَرَآئَۃِ مِمَّنْ اَسَّسَ اَسَاسَ الظُّلْمِ وَالْجَوْرِ عَلَیْكُمْ \nWA BIL-BARAAA-ATE MIMMAN ASSASA ASAASAZ ZULME WAL JAWRE A’LAYKUM \nand those who established the foundations of tyranny, and wrongs against you (O Ahl al-Bayt).\nوَاَبْرَءُ اِلَی اللهِ وَ اِلٰی رَسُوْلِهٖ مِمَّنْ اَسَّسَ اَسَاسَ ذٰلِكَ وَبَنی عَلَیْهِ بُنْیَانَهٗ\nWA ABRAO ELAL LAAHE WA ELAA RASOOLEHEE MIMMAN ASSASA ASAASA ZAALEKA WA BANAA A’LAYHE BUNYAANAHU \nI turn to Allah, and His Messenger, disassociating with those who laid grounds for it, and those who built upon it,\nوَ جَرٰی فِیْ ظُلْمِهٖ وَ جَوْرِهٖ عَلَیْكُمْ\nWA JARAA FEE ZULMEHEE WA JAWREHI A’LAYKUM \nand carried out oppression and cruelty, on you \nوَ عَلی اَشْیَاعِكُمْ بَرِئْتُ اِلَی اللهِ وَ اِلَیْكُمْ مِنْهُمْ\nWA A’LAA ASHYAA-E’KUM BAREA’TO ELAL LAAHE WA ELAYKUM MINHUM \nand your followers. I disassociate myself from them,\nوَ اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَی اللهِ ثُمَّ اِلَیْكُمْ\nWA ATAQARRABO ELAL LAAHE SUMMA ELAYKUM \nand seek nearness to Allah, and then to you \nبِمُوَالَاتِكُمْ وَ مُوَالَاۃِ وَ لِیِّكُمْ\nBE-MAWAALAATEKUM WA MOWAALAATE WALIYYEKUM \nthrough love for you and your friends,\nوَ بِالْبَرَآئَۃِ مِنْ اَعْدَائِكُمْ\nWA BIL-BARAAA-ATE MIN AA’-DAAA-EKUM \nand disassociation with your enemies, \nوَ النَّاصِبِیْنَ لَكُمُ الْحَرْبَ\nWAN NAASEBEENA LAKOMUL HARBA \nand from those who went to war with you,\nوَ بِالْبَرَائَۃِ مِنْ اَشْیَاعِهِمْ وَ اَتْبَاعِهِمْ\nWA BIL BARAAA-ATE MIN ASHYAA-E’HIM WA ATBAA-E’HIM \ntheir adherents and their followers.\nاِنِّی سِلْمٌ لِمَنْ سَالَمَكُمْ\nINNEE SILMUN LEMAN SAALAMAKUM \nI am at peace with those who made peace with you, \nوَ حَرْبٌ لِمَنْ حَارَبَكُمْ\nWA HARBUN LEMAN HAARABAKUM \nand I am at war with those who went to war with you.\nوَ وَلِیٌّ لِمَنْ وَالَاكُمْ\nWA WALIYYUN LEMAN WAALAAKUM \nI befriend those who befriended you, \nوَ عَدُوٌّ لِمَنْ عَادَاكُمْ\nWA A’DUWWUN LEMAN A’ADAAKUM \nand I am at enmity with those who were your enemies.\nفَاَسْئَلُ اللهَ الَّذِیْ اَكْرَمَنِیْ بِمَعْرِفَتِكُمْ\nFA-AS-ALUL LAAHAL LAZEE AKRAMANEE BE MAA’REFATEKUM \nI pray to Allah, who has honored me with awareness of you,\nوَ مَعْرِفَۃِ اَوْلِیَآئِكُمْ\nWA MAA’REFATE AWLEYAAAEKUM \nand awareness of your friends\nوَ رَزَقَنِیَ الْبَرَآئَۃَ مِنْ اَعْدَآئِكُمْ\nWA RAZAQANIL BARAAA-ATA MIN AA’-DAAA-EKUM \nand has enabled me to withdraw from your enemies.\nاَنْ یَجْعَلَنِیْ مَعَكُمْ فِیْ الدُّنْیَا وَ اْلآخِرَۃِ\nWA ANY YAJ-A’LANEE MA-A’KUM FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE \n(I pray) that He may place me with you in this world and the Hereafter.\nوَ اَنْ یُثَبِّتَ لِی عِنْدَ كُمْ قَدَمَ صِدْقٍ\nWA ANY YOSABBETA LEE I’NDAKUM QADAMA SIDQIN \nAnd (I pray) that He may strengthen for me a truthful stance \nفِیْ الدُّنْیَا وَ اْلآخِرَۃِ\nFID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE \nin this world and the Hereafter.\nوَ اَسْئَلُهُ اَنْ یُبَلِّغَنِی الْمَقَامَ الْمَحْمُوْدَ لَكُمْ عِنْدَ اللهِ\nWA AS-ALOHU ANY YOBALLEGHANIL MAQAAMAL MAHMOODA LAKUM I’NDAL LAAHE \nAnd I pray that He may enable me to reach, your honoured station with Allah\nوَ اَنْ یَرْزُقَنِیْ طَلَبَ ثَارِیْ \nWA ANY YARZOQANEE TALABA SAAREE \nand that He may grant me the opportunity to seek victory, \nمَعَ اِمَامٍ هُدًی ظَاهِرٍ نَاطِقٍ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْكُمْ\nMA-A’ EMAAMIN HODAN ZAAHERIN NAATEQIN BIL-HAQQE MINKUM \nalong with a rightly guided Imam from amongst you, who will surely come and speak the truth.\nوَ اَسْئَلُ اللهَ بِحَقِّكُمْ وَ بِالشَّانِ الَّذِیْ لَكُمْ عِنْدَهٗ\nWA AS-ALUL LAAHA BE-HAQQEKUM WA BISH-SHAANIL LAZEE LAKUM I’NDAHU \nI ask Allah for your sake, and by the honoured position you have with Him,\nاَنْ یُعْطِیَنِیْ بِمُصَابِیْ بِكُمْ اَفْضَلَ مَا یُعْطِیْ مُصَابًا بِمُصِیْبَتِهٖ\nANY YOA’-TEYANEE BE-MOSAABEE BEKUM AFZALA MAA YOA’-TEE MOSAABAN BE-MOSEEBATIN \nthat He grants me grief at your sorrows, more than the personal grief that troubles anyone in tragedy.\nمُصِیْبَۃً مَا اَعْظَمَهَا\nMOSEEBATAN MAA AA’-ZAMAHAA \nWhat great sorrows (you experienced)!\nوَ اَعْظَمَ رَزِیَّتَهَا فِیْ اْلاِسْلَامِ\nWA AA’-ZAMA RAZIYYATAHAA FIL ISLAAME \nHow great was your tragedy for Islam, \nوَ فِیْ جَمِیْعِ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَ اْلأَرْضِ\nWA FEE JAMEE-I’S SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ \nand all the Heavens and the earth!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِیْ فِیْ مَقَامِیْ هٰذَا مِمَّنْ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A’LNEE FEE MAQAAMEE HAAZAA MIMMAN \nO Allah, make me, at this moment, \nتَنَالُهٗ مِنْكَ صَلَوَاتٌ وَ رَحْمَۃٌ وَ مَغْفِرَۃٌ\nTANAALOHU MINKA SALAWAATUN WA RAHMATUN WA MAGHFERATUN \none who receives from You, blessings, mercy, and forgiveness.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ مَحْیَایَ مَحْیَا مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMAJ-A'L MAHYAAYA MAHYAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nO Allah make me live the life of Muhammad (s.a.w.a.) and his family\nوَ مَمَاتِیْ مَمَاتَ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA MAMAATEE MAMAATA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nand make me die the death of Muhammad (s.a.w.a.) and his family.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذَا یَوْمٌ تَبَرَّكَتْ بِهٖ بَنُوْ اُمَیَّۃَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAAZAA YAWMUN TABARRAKAT BEHI BANOO UMAYYATA \nO my Allah this day is a day of rejoicing for the Bani Umayyah, \nوَابْنُ آكِلَۃِ الْأَكُبَادِ اللَّعِیْنُ ابْنُ اللَّعِیْنِ عَلٰی لِسَانِكَ\nWABNO AAKELATIL AKBAADIL LA-E'ENUBNUL LA-E'ENE A'LAA LESAANEKA \nthe herd of hardened criminals, the eternally damned and accursed group, a fact that had been made public by Thee \nوَ لِسَانِ نَبِیِّكَ صَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَآلِهٖ\nWA LESAANE NABIYYEKA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI\nand Your Prophet, blessings of Allah be on him and his family,\nفِیْ كُلِّ مَوْطِنٍ وَ مَوْقِفٍ وَ قَفَ فِیْهِ نَبِیُّكَ صَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ آلِهٖ\nFEE KULLE MAWTENIN WA MAWQEFIN WAQAFA FEEHE NABIYYOKA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \nWho (blessings of Allah be on him and his family), in every place and at all occasions, drew attention of people to this truism.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنْ اَبَا سُفْیَانَ وَ مُعَاوِیَۃَ\nALLAAHUMMAAL-A'N ABAA SUFYAAN WA MO-A'AWEYATA \nO Allah, curse Abu Sufyan, Mu`awiya, \nوَ یَزِیْدَ بْنَ مُعَاوِیَۃَ\nWA YAZEEDABNA MO-A'AWEYATA \nand Yazíd son of Mu`awiya \nعَلَیْهِمْ مِنْكَ اللَّعْنَۃُ اَبَدَ الْآبِدِیْنَ\nA'LAYHIM MINKAL LA’NATO ABADAL AABEDEENA \nlet it be an everlasting curse upon them from Thee.\nوَ هٰذَا یَوْمٌ فَرِحَتْ بِهٖ آلُ زِیادٍ وَ آلُ مَرْوَانَ\nWA HAAZAA YAWMUN FAREHAT BEHI AALO ZEYAADIN WA AALO MARWAANA \nAnd this is a day when the family of Ziyad was happy, and the family of Marwan, \nبِقَتْلِهِمُ الْحُسَیْنَ صَلَوٰاتُ اللهِ عَلَیْهِ\nBE-QATLEHEMUL HUSAYNA SALAWAATUL LAAHE A'LAYHHE \nbecause of their murder of Husayn, blessings of Allah be on him.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَضَاعِفْ عَلَیْهِمُ الَّعْنَ مِنْكَ وَ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAZAA-I’F A’LAYHEMUL LA’NA MINKA WAL A’ZAABAL ALEEMA \nO Allah, so increase the curse on them from You, and the painful punishment.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَیْكَ فِیْ هٰذَا الْیَوْمِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ATAQARRABO ELAYKA FEE HAAZAL YAWME \nO Allah, I seek nearness to You on this day, \nوَ فِیْ مَوْقِفِیْ هٰذَا وَ اَیَّامِ حَیٰوتِیْ\nWA FEE MAWQEFEE HAAZAA WA AYYAAME HAYAATEE \nand in this position, and for the rest of my life, \nبِالْبَرَآئَۃِ مِنْهُمْ وَ اللَّعْنَۃِ عَلَیْهِمْ\nBIL-BARAAA-ATE MINHUM WAL LA’NATE A’LAYHIM\nthrough disassociating with them (the enemies) and cursing them,\nوَ بِالْمُوَالَاتِ لِنَبِیِّكَ وَ آلِ نَبِیِّكَ\nWA BIL MOWAALAATE LE-NABIYYEKA WA AALE NABIYYEKA \nand through the love of Your Prophet, \nعَلَیْهِ وَ عَلِیْهِمُ السَّلَامُ\nA’LAYHE WA A’LAYHEMUS SALAAMO.\nand his family, peace be on them.\nThen say 100 times:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنْ اَوّلَ ظَالِمٍ ظَلَمَ حَقَّ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMAL A’N AWWALA ZAALEMIN ZALAMA HAQQA MOHAMMADIN \nO Allah, curse the first tyrant who oppressed, the right of Muhammad\nوَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آخِرَ تَابِعٍ لَهٗ عَلٰی ذٰلِكَ\nWA AALE MOHAMMADIN WA AAKHERA TAABE-I'N LAHU A'LAA ZAALEKA \nand his family, and the next who followed him on that.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنِ الْعِصَابَۃَ الَّتِیْ جَاهَدَتِ الْحُسَیْنَ\nALLAAHUMMAL-A'NIL E'SAABATAL LATEE JAAHADATIL HUSAYNA \nO Allah, curse the group who fought Husayn,\nوَ شَایَعَتْ وَ بایَعَتْ وَ تَابَعَتْ عَلٰی قَتْلِهٖ\nWA SHAAYA-A'T WA BAA-YA-A'T WA TAA-BA-A'T A'LAA QATLEHI\nand the group which followed and supported, and joined hands to kill him.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنْهُمْ جَمِیْعًا\nALLAHUMMAL-A'NHUM JAMEE-A'N.\nO Allah curse them all\nThen again say 100 times:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ\nASSALAAMO A'LAYKA YAA ABAA A'BDILLAAHE \nPeace be on You O Abu Abdillah\nوَ عَلَی الْأَرْوَاحِ الَّتِیْ حَلَّتْ بِفِنَآئِكَ\nWA A'LAL ARWAAHIL LATEE HALLAT BEFENAA-EKA \nand on the souls that died with you.\nعَلَیْكَ مِنّی سَلَامُ اللهِ اَبَدًا\nA'LAYKA MINNE SALAAMUL LAAHE ABADAM \nGreetings of Peace of Allah be on you, from me, forever so long as I live \nمَا بَقِیْتُ وَ بَقِيَ اللَّیْلُ وَ النَّهَارُ\nMAA BAQEETO WA BAQEYAL LAYLO WAN NAHAARO \nand so long as the night and day remain.\nوَ لَا جَعَلَهُ اللهُ آخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنِّی لِزِیَارَتِكُمْ\nWA LAA JA-A'LAHUL LAAHO AAKHERAL A’HDE MINNEE LE-ZEYAARATEKUM \nMay Allah not make it my last contact of ziyarat with you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَی الْحُسَیْنِ\nASSALAAMO A'LAL HUSAYNE \nPeace be on Husayn, \nوَ عَلٰی عَلِیِّ بْنِ الْحُسَیْنِ\nWA A'LAA A'LIYYIBNIL HUSAYNE \nand on Ali the son of Husayn,\nوَ عَلٰی اَوْلادِ الْحُسَیْنِ\nWA A'LAA AWLAADIL HUSAYNE \nAnd on the children of Husayn \nوَ عَلٰی اَصْحَابِ الْحُسَیْنِ\nWA A'LAA ASHAABIL HUSAYNE\nand the companions of Husayn,\nThen say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ خُصَّ اَنْتَ اَوَّلَ ظَالِمٍ بِاللَّعْنِ مِنِّی\nALLAAHUMMA KHUSSA ANTA AWWALA ZAALEMIN BIL-LA'NE MINNEE \nO my Allah, let the curse I call down on the head of the first tyrant stick like a leech;\nوَابْدَأْ بِهٖ اَوَّلًا\nWAB DAA BEHI AWWALAN \nand stay put for ever on the first,\nثُمَّ الثَّانِيَۃْ وَ الثَّالِثَ وَالرَّابِعْ\nSUMMAS SAANEYA WAS SAALESA WAR RAABE’\nthen the second, the third, and the fourth.\nاَللَّهُمَّ الْعَنْ یَزِیْدَ خَامِسًا\nALLAAHUMMAL-A'N YAZEEDA KHAAMESAN \nO Allah, curse the fifth one, Yazíd, \nوَ الْعَنْ عُبَیْدَ اللهِ بْنِ زِیَادٍ وَابْنَ مَرْجَانَۃَ\nWAL A'N O'BAYDAL LAAH IBNA ZEYAADIN WAB NA MARJAANAH \nand Ubaidallah bin Ziyad, Ibne Marjanah, \nوَ عُمَرَبْنَ سَعْدٍ وَ شِمْرًا\nWA O'MAR ABNA SA'DIN WA SHIMRAN \nand Umar ibne Sa’d, and Shimr, \nوَ آلَ أَبِيْ سُفْیَانَ وَ آلَ زِیَادٍ\nWA AALA ABEE SUFYAANA WA AALA ZEYAADIN \nand the family of Abu Sufyan, the family of Ziyad, \nوَ آلَ مَرْوَانَ اِلٰی یَوْمِ الْقِیَامَۃِ.\nWA AALA MARWAANA ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE.\nand the family of Marwan, till the Day of Judgement\nThen go in Sajdah and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ حَمْدَ الشَّاكِرِیْنَ لَكَ عَلٰی مُصَابِهِمْ\nALLAAHUMMA LAKAL HAMDO HAMDASH SHAAKEREENA LAKA A'LAA MOSAABEHIM \nO Allah, for You is Praise, Praise of those who are thankful to You (even) during tragedy.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلهِ عَلٰی عَظِیْمِ رَزِیَّتِیْ\nALHAMDO LILLAAHE A'LAA A'ZEEME RAZIYYATEE \nPraise be to Allah for my intense grief\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنِیْ شَفَاعَۃَ الْحُسَیْنِ یَوْمَ الْوُرُوْدِ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNEE SHAFAA-A'TAL HUSAYNE YAWMAL WOROODE \nO Allah, grant me the intercession of Husayn, on the Day of appearance (before You),\nوَ ثَبِّتْ لِیْ قَدَمَ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَكَ\nWA SABBIT LEE QADAMA SIDQIN I’NDAKA \nand strengthen for me a truthful stand with You, \nمَعَ الْحُسَیْنِ وَ اَصْحَابِ الْحُسَیْنِ الَّذِیْنَ \nMA-A'L HUSAYNE WA ASHAABIL HUSAYNIL LAZEENA \nwith Husayn and the companions of Husayn,\nبَذَلُوْا مُهَجَهُمْ دُوْنَ الْحُسَیْنِ عَلَیْهِ السَّلَامُ.\nBAZALOO MOHAJAHUM DOONAL HUSAYNE A'LAYHIS SALAAMO.\nwho sacrificed everything, for Husayn, peace be on him.\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t    ",
  "merits": "Importance of Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora\nThe virtues and merits of Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora can be best understood based on the traditions of the Holy Infalliables (a.s.) which have been narrated regarding its importance and recitation. There are many incidents by which the importance of this Ziyaarat is realized . \nThe Ziyaarat is followed by 2 rakaats namaaz and a dua known as Dua-e-Alqamah which Imam Sadiq (a.s.) used to recite after Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora and he also taught the same to his companion Alqamah (r.a.).\nZiyaarat-e-Ashoora: In the light of traditions\nThe importance and merits of reciting Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora can be understood from the following traditions:\nTradition 1\nAlqamah bin Mohammed ibn Hazrami (r.a.) narrates ‘I requested Imam Baqir (a.s.) to teach me a dua that I should recite on the day of Ashoora after the reciting the Ziyaarat of Imam Husain (a.s.) - from near his (a.s.) grave or from a distance.’ Imam (a.s.) replied\n‘O Alqamah, whenever you wish to recite the Ziyaarat of Imam Husain (a.s.), you first perform two units of prayers. Then turn towards the grave of Imam Husain (a.s.) and while pointing towards it, you first say ‘Salam’ and then ‘Takbeer’. Thereafter, you recite this Ziyaarat (Ziyaarat-e-Aashura). If you do so, then as if you have recited the supplication read by the angels while visiting the grave of Imam Husain (a.s.). Moreover, when you recite this Ziyaarat, then\n(a)\tAllah will record a million good deeds for you, erase a million sins and add a hundred million ranks to your rank.\n(b)\tYou will be included among those people who were martyred along with Imam Husain (a.s.) and you will share their ranks.\n(c)\tOn the day of Judgment, you will be included among the martyrs\n(d)\tYou will get the reward of all the Prophets, Messengers and all the people who have visited the grave of Imam Husain (a.s.) from the day that he (a.s.) was martyred till date.\nAnd the way of reciting the Ziyaarat is like this…’\n(Then Imam (a.s.) recited the entire Ziyaarat-e-Ashura for Alqamah (r.a.))\n(Kaamil al-Ziyarat, Ibn Qoolwayh, Ch. 71, p.194)\nAt the end of this tradition, Imam Baqir (a.s.) says:\n‘O Alqamah, if you can, then recite this Ziyaarat every day send salutations to Imam Husain (a.s.). You will get all the rewards (of the one who recites it on the day of Ashoora).’\nTradition 2\nImam Sadiq (a.s.) informs,\n‘The one who does the Ziyaarat of Imam Husain (a.s.) on the day of Ashoora, then paradise is obligatory upon him.’\n(Behaar al-Anwaar, vol. 101, p.104)\nZiyarat-e-Ashoora: Hadees-e-Qudsi\nThe greatest merit for this Ziyaarat is that it is the ‘Word of Allah’ (Hadees-e-Qudsi). Safwan (r.a.) narrates that Hazrat Jibraeel (a.s.) conveyed this Ziyaarat to Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) on divine command and it has reached Imam Baqir (a.s.) through his noble ancestors.\nZiyaarat-e-Ashoora: Emphasis of Imam-e-Zamana (a.t.f.s.)\nThe emperor of the era, the chief of the universe, Imam-e-Zamana (a.t.f.s.) has stressed the importance of reciting Ziyarat-e-Ashoora.\nShaykh Mohaddis Noori (r.a.) in his book “Najmus Saqib” writes that there was a person called Syed Ahmed Rashty who was on his way to Hajj with his companions.\nIt was winter and one night there was snow and ice accompanied by strong winds. \nSyed Ahmed got separated from his companions. \nHe says he was trembling with fear and cold as it was a place where people often looted.  Suddenly he saw a person with a shovel freeing the tree branches which were burdened with snow. The man greeted Syed Ahmed saying “Assalamu Alaykum Syed Ahmed! Where are you going?” Amazed at the person knowing his name he said he was on his way to Hajj but had lost his way.  The man told him “Alayka bin Nafela! Nafela! Nafela!” Syed Ahmed prayed his Maghrib and Isha salaah finishing each with its Nafela.  He saw the man again who asked him, “Have you not gone yet?” Syed Ahmed replied “No!” The man said, “Alayka bil Jaameah! Jaameah! Jaameah!”\nSyed Ahmed says that I did not know Ziyarat-e-Jameah by heart but that day I could recite it as though I had memorised it. The man told him, “Alayka bil Ashoora! Ashoora! Ashoora!”\nSyed Ahmed recited Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora and Dua Alqamah. The man then mounted on his horse and took him to his caravan and the companions he had been separated from.\nAs he parted Imam (a.t.f.s.) said to Syed Ahmed, “REMEMBER ZIYAARAT-E-ASHOORA, THERE IS NO GREATER GIFT THAN IT.” \nWe see how Imam-e-Zamana (a.t.f.s.) helped Syed Ahmed and stressed upon the recitation of Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora. It also points to the fact that Imam-e-Zamana (a.t.f.s.) desires that his followers should always remember the tribulations of his grandfather Imam Husain (a.s.) and they should always be aggrieved and anguished by the events of Karbala.\nSafwan's Discourse on the Merit of Ziyaarat of Ashoora\nSayf ibn Umayrah has reported that he said to Safwan, “Alqamah ibn Muhammad has not reported this supplication to us from Imam al-Baqir (a.s.). He has only reported the ziyarah form.”\nAnswering him, Safwan said:\nI once accompanied my master al-Sadiq, Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, to this very place. He did as same as we have just done as regarding the method of ziyarah and then, after offering a prayer similar to the one we have just offered and bidding the visited Imam farewell as same as we have done, he said this very supplication.\nSafwan added, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said to me, “Observe this form of ziyarah and this supplication and use them whenever you visit (the Imam). Surely, I guarantee on behalf of Almighty Allah for any one who says this form of ziyarah and this supplication while visiting the holy tomb or being at a distant place that his visit will be accepted, his efforts will be praiseworthy, his greetings will reach the Imams and will never be screened from them, all his requests will be granted by Almighty Allah whatever they will be, and he will never be disappointed. O Safwan, the Imam (a.s.) added, I have received this very guarantee for those who use this form of ziyarah when visiting the holy tombs from my father who received it from his father Ali ibn al-Husayn (a.s.) who received it from his father al-Husayn (a.s.) who received it from his brother al-Hasan (a.s.) who received it from his father the Commander of the Faithful who received it from the Messenger of Allah who received it from Archangel Jibraeel who received it from Almighty Allah, Who undertook for any one who would visit Imam al-Husayn (‘a) with this form of ziyarah and say this very supplication from the holy shrine or from a distant place that He (i.e. Almighty Allah) Himself should accept his visitation, grant him his requests whatever they would be, and respond to his prayers. Moreover, the visitor should never leave with disappointment; rather, Almighty Allah should make him leave with pleasure and delight of his eye due to settling of his needs, winning Paradise, being manumitted from Hellfire, and being granted the right to intercede for whomever he wishes except those who openly incur the animosity of the Ahl al-Bayt (a.s.). Almighty Allah, as was maintained by Archangel Gabriel, undertook this pledge and called the angels to witness for it after the angels of His Kingdom had witnessed the same. O Allah’s Messenger, Archangel Gabriel added, Almighty Allah has sent me to carry this pleasant and good tidings to you as well as to Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, the Imams from your descendants, and your adherents (i.e. Shi'ah) up to the Resurrection Day. Up to the Resurrection Day, you as well as ‘Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, and your adherents shall be pleased.\nSafwan added, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) then said to me: O Safwan, whenever you have an impenetrable problem that cannot be solved except by Almighty Allah, you must then visit (Imam al-Husayn) with this form of ziyarah, wherever you would be, and follow it with this supplication. You may then beseech your Lord to grant you your request and the response shall soon come from Almighty Allah Who never fails in His promise to His Messenger; out of His magnanimity and favoring. All praise be then to Allah.\nMore Confirmations\nIn the book of al-Najm al-Saaqib (by al-Nuri), the story of the attendance of Hajj Sayyid Ahmad al-Rashti in the presence of the Imam of the Age, may our souls be accepted as ransoms from him, during his journey of the hajj pilgrimage, has been told in details. In one of the details of this story, which will be cited in this book after the Major Comprehensive Form of ziyaarah (al-Ziyaarah al-Jaamea;h al-Kabeerah), the Imam (a.s.) said to al-Rashti with confirmation, “Why do you not (frequently) recite the ziyarah of ‘Ashoora’, ‘Ashoora’, ‘Ashoora’, ‘Ashoora’...?”\nCommenting on this, our trustworthy mentor Shaykh al-Nuri said:\nOne of the unparalleled merits and points of honor of ziyarah of ‘Ashura’ is that its form is not similar to the other ordinary forms of ziyarah, which have been composed and dictated by the Holy Infallibles apparently, although nothing is issued from the immaculate hearts of these Holy Infallibles except statements proving that they have received these words from the Most High Origin. The ziyarah of ‘Ashura’, however, is similar to the Words of Almighty Allah that He revealed to Archangel Jibraeel. This fact can be noticed in the words of this form of ziyarah, including the statements of invoking curses (on the enemies), the statements of invoking blessings (on the Imam and his companions), and the supplicatory statements. Hence, Archangel Jibraeel conveyed these words to the Seal of the Prophets. As maintained by tangible experiences, this form of ziyarah is unique in achieving the requests, gaining the needs, and warding off the enemies if a visitor recites it continuously for forty days or even less. However, the most astonishing effect of preserving in reciting this form of ziyarah can be touched in the following story, mentioned in the book of Dar al-Salam. However, I will mention it in brief:\nHasan al-Yazdi the trustworthy, righteous, and pious Hajj and Mawla who lived in the vicinity of the holy shrine in al-Ghari (i.e. al-Najaf) and who was one of those who acted faithfully as regards neighboring this holy place and practiced acts of worship painstakingly, has reported the following incident from Muhammad ‘Ali al-Yazdi the trustworthy and honest Hajj:\nIn Yazd, there was a righteous and virtuous man who used to preoccupy himself (with acts of worship) and make preparations for his next life in his grave. He used to spend nights in a graveyard in the skirts of the city of Yazd, known as Mazar, in which a group of righteous people were buried. He had a neighbor who grew up with him since infanthood and both joined the same school and studied under the same mentor. Nevertheless, this neighbor became a tither (i.e. he seizes tenth of the people’s gains by means of power and injustice). He did not quit this process until he died. He was then buried in that graveyard in a grave near the place where the righteous man used to stay overnight.\nIn less than one month after the death of this tither, his righteous neighbor saw him in sleep in a good-looking costume as if he was enjoying the brightness of bliss. The righteous man approached the dead man and asked him, “I know very well your origin and your end, and your open appearance and your hidden manners. You were not one of those whom are expected to have righteous inner self and your deeds would bring you nothing but torment and chastisement. How could you attain this status?”\nThe dead replied, “What you have just said is exactly the truth. I had been placed in the most terrible torture since my death up to yesterday when the wife of Ashraf, the blacksmith, died and was buried in this place.” The dead pointed to a definite side, which was about one hundred arms away from his burial place. He then went on, “At the night of her burial, Abu-’Abdullah (Imam al-Husayn) visited her three times. In the third time, he ordered torture to be stopped from all the dead inhabitants of this graveyard. Since then, I was turned into bliss, luxury, comfort, and coziness.”\nWhen the righteous man woke up, he was deeply perplexed. He therefore went to the market of the blacksmiths to ask about the man whose wife had recently died, because he had no familiarity with that man. When he found the blacksmith, he asked him, “Did you have a wife?” The blacksmith answered, “Yes, I had. She died recently and she was buried in such-and-such place.” The man mentioned the very place to which the dead tither pointed in the dream of the righteous man. “Had she ever visited the tomb of Abu-’Abdullah?” the righteous man asked. “No, she had not,” answered her widower. “Did she usually mention the misfortunes that the Imam (a.s.) had to encounter?” asked the righteous man. “No, she did not,” answered her widower. “Was she usually holding consolation ceremonies for Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)?” asked the righteous man. “No, she was not,” answered her widower, who added, “What for are you putting such questions?” Here, the righteous man narrated the whole story of his dream. The widower then said, “Yes, she used to recite ziyarah of ‘Ashura’ very frequently.”\nWe pray to Allah – the Almighty – that He includes us among the fortunate ones – those who have the taufeeq of reciting Ziyaarat-e-Ashoora regularly."
}
